            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "LinguisticObject",
      "content": "<p>Coleman Sellers (1781-1834) married Rembrandt Peale's sister, Sofonisba Anguissola (1786-1859), in 1805. Sellers, an engineer and inventor, financed several of Peale’s European trips, taken to further the artist’s education and career. This painting was probably completed shortly after Seller’s unexpected death; an earlier version of the work (private collection) was completed in 1832.</p>\n",
      "classified_as": [
